**5. Shared Mental Model & Future Coordination:**
- The team's shared understanding is now that I (P1) have a known, playable card.
- I am expected to play Card 4 on my next turn. This will advance the fireworks and keep the game moving.
- P2 anticipates this play and will likely plan their next turn around it, probably by discarding a less critical card from their hand (like G4 or W4, which are not yet playable) to generate a new clue for the team. This clue will be vital for saving the important 5s and other key cards in our hands.

